<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Msallata</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Masallata</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Msallata is a town in the hills of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, inland from Khoms and south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli</a>. In November 1918, after the Ottoman defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, Tripolitanian notables gathered there and proclaimed the Tripolitanian Republic, one of the first republics of the Arab world. Its leaders took advantage of the fact that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> then held little more than the coastal towns of Libya.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/msallata.jpg" alt="Msallata" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hakeem.gadi · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Horizon_shot_in_Msallata-Libya01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
